<title>USA: World Bank projections for Latam current accounts.</title>
<headline>World Bank projections for Latam current accounts.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The World Bank's Latin America and Caribbean division released Wednesday its lead economists' working numbers on current account balances for the region.</p>
<p>The following is a table of those non official projections, in percentages of GDP.</p>
<p> COUNTRY		1996	   1997	   1998</p>
<p> Argentina	   (2.2)	  (2.6)	  (2.7)</p>
<p> Belize		(4.9)	  (3.1)	  (2.3)</p>
<p> Bolivia	     (8.8)	  (9.7)	  (8.7)</p>
<p> Brazil		(2.6)	  (2.6)	  (2.3)</p>
<p> Chile		 (3.0)	  (2.5)	  (2.0)</p>
<p> Colombia	    (5.6)	  (5.2)	  (4.9)</p>
<p> Costa Rica	  (2.3)	  (2.2)	  (2.7)</p>
<p> Dominican Rep	0.0	    0.0	    0.0</p>
<p> Ecuador	     (3.9)	  (3.4)	  (2.6)</p>
<p> El Salvador	 (4.7)	  (4.4)	  (4.0)</p>
<p> Guatemala	   (5.0)	  (4.5)	  (4.5)</p>
<p> Guyana		(9.0)	  (9.0)	  (9.0)</p>
<p> Haiti		(17.0)	 (15.8)	 (14.1)</p>
<p> Honduras	    (5.6)	  (6.1)	  (5.8)</p>
<p> Jamaica	     (4.0)	  (2.0)	   1.0</p>
<p> Mexico		(1.2)	  (1.6)	  (1.9)</p>
<p> Nicaragua	  (29.6)	 (23.0)	 (20.7)</p>
<p> Panama		(4.2)	  (4.2)	  (4.0)</p>
<p> Paraguay	   (13.6)	 (13.3)	 (12.0)</p>
<p> Peru		  (5.7)	  (5.4)	  (4.8)</p>
<p> Trinidad	     1.5	    2.5	    1.1</p>
<p> Uruguay	     (1.9)	  (1.6)	  (1.8)</p>
<p> Venezuela	    4.3	    2.1	    1.3</p>
<p>-- IMF newsroom (202) 842-2124</p>
